@startuml SD-5b
!include ../_style.iuml
title SD-5b (Software level, CSMS) — Charge Point connects for the first time and goes into service\nPrecondition: Charge Point is awaiting_connection · System view: AD-8 · State: STM-3, STM-2
footer Owner: Trần Đức Ân (WP1) · v2.0 · 01/11/2026 · names = code after the Charge Point rename (T90) · left gate = Charge Point [OCPP 1.6J, WSS]

participant "«component»\n<u>:OcppServer</u>" as OS
participant "«component»\n<u>:ChargePointAuthService</u>" as PA
participant "«component»\n<u>:ChargePointLifecyclePolicy</u>" as PLP
participant "«component»\n<u>:ConnectionRegistry</u>" as REG
participant "«component»\n<u>:OcppHandlers</u>" as H
participant "«component»\n<u>:SessionsService</u>" as S

[-> OS ++ : WebSocket upgrade /ocpp/{serial}, Basic auth [WSS, TLS]
OS -> PA ++ : verify(identity, password, clientIp) : decision
PA -> PA : find Charge Point, check login limit,\ncompare credential hash
PA -> PLP ++ : mayConnect(lifecycle) : boolean
PLP --> PA --
PA --> OS -- : accept | reject
break unknown serial, not onboarded, or wrong credential
  [<-- OS : HTTP 404 / 403 / 401, connection refused (attempt logged)
end
OS -> REG ++ : open(identity, client) : Connection
REG -> REG : new epoch, is_online = true,\nawaiting_connection → in_service (FIRST_CONNECT)
note right : set in SQL, not through\nChargePointLifecyclePolicy (CD-5 note)
REG --> OS --
[<-- OS -- : 101 Switching Protocols
hnote over REG : {chargePoint.lifecycle = in_service}

[-> OS ++ : BootNotification {vendor, model, firmwareVersion}
OS -> H ++ : dispatch(BootNotification, params, ctx)
H --> OS -- : {Accepted, currentTime, interval}
[<-- OS -- : BootNotification.conf {Accepted, interval}

loop for each connector
  [-> OS ++ : StatusNotification {connectorId, Available}
  OS -> H ++ : dispatch(StatusNotification, params, ctx)
  H -> S ++ : onStatusNotification(req, ctx)
  S -> S : connector Unavailable → Available
  S --> H --
  H --> OS --
  [<-- OS -- : StatusNotification.conf {}
end
note over OS, S : The Charge Point now appears on the driver map and on the Operator dashboard. Reading capabilities (reservation support, battery level, free-vend tag) after boot is design (AD-8), not in code yet.
@enduml
